      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-183478",
      ":question/problem": "Using the formal definition of a limit, prove that\n\n$lim_(n \u2192 \u221e)\\frac{3^{n + 1} + 1}{3^{n} - 2} = 3$.\n\nWe need to show that for any real $\u03b5 > 0$, there exists a natural number $N$ such that, for every natural number $n \\ge N$, we have\n\n$\\mid \\frac{3^{n + 1} + 1}{3^{n} - 2} - 3 \\mid < \u03b5$.\n\nSolving this inequality for $n$, we get\n$>$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\n\nTherefore, we choose $N$\n{{field-3}} {{field-4}}."
